le":"Pronouns","text":["Kyrgyz often drops the pronoun, because the verb ending shows who is speaking. There is no he / she difference: \"ал\" means both."],"rows":[["I","мен","men"],["you (informal)","сен","sen"],["he / she / it","ал","al"],["we","биз","beez"],["you (formal or plural)","сиз","seez"],["they","алар","ah-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am a student","мен студентмин","men stoo-dent-MEEN"],["you are tall","сен узунсуң","sen oo-zoon-SOONG"],["she is my older sister","ал менин эжем","al meh-NIN eh-ZHEM"],["we are friends","биз достубуз","beez dos-too-BOOZ"],["they are teachers","алар мугалимдер","ah-LAR moo-gah-leem-DER"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Add -лар, -лер, -дар, -дер, -тар, -тер or -лор, -лөр, by vowel harmony and the last sound. After a number, the noun stays singular: эки китеп (two book)."],"rows":[["китеп (book)","китептер","kee-tep-TER"],["үй (house)","үйлөр","ewy-LUR"],["бала (child)","балдар","bal-DAR"],["after a number: singular","эки китеп","eh-KEE kee-TEP"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","бир үй, үйлөр","beer EWY ewy-LUR"],["one book, books","бир китеп, китептер","beer kee-TEP kee-tep-TER"],["one cat, cats","бир мышык, мышыктар","beer muh-SHUHK muh-shuhk-TAR"],["two books","эки китеп","eh-KEE kee-TEP"],["the children","балдар","bal-DAR"]]},{"id":"to-be","title":"To be: -мын, -сың, -быз","text":["There is no separate verb \"to be\". Add an ending to the noun or adjective. The ending changes by vowel harmony and the last sound: -мын / -мин / -бын / -бин / -пын / -пин."],"rows":[["I am","-мын / -мин","muhn"],["you are","-сың / -сиң","suhng"],["he / she is","(no ending)","-"],["we are","-быз / -биз","buhz"],["you are (formal)","-сыз / -сиз","suhz"],["they are","-лар / -лер","lar"]],"ex":[["I am a student","мен студентмин","men stoo-dent-MEEN"],["you are tired","сен чарчагансың","sen char-chah-gan-SUHNG"],["he is a doctor","ал дарыгер","al dah-ruh-GER"],["we are happy","биз бактылуубуз","beez bak-tuh-loo-BOOZ"],["they are at home","алар үйдө","ah-LAR ewy-DUR"]]},{"id":"bar-and-jok-have-there-is","title":"Bar and jok: have, there is","text":["Kyrgyz says \"at me there is\" (бар) or \"at me there is not\" (жок). The ending -да / -де means \"at\" or \"in\"."],"rows":[["there is","бар","bar"],["there is not","жок","zhok"],["I have","менде ... бар","men-DEH bar"],["I do not have","менде ... жок","men-DEH zhok"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","менде аке бар","men-DEH ah-KEH bar"],["I have a car","менде машина бар","men-DEH mah-SHEE-nah bar"],["I do not have time","менде убакыт жок","men-DEH oo-bah-KUHT zhok"],["there is a problem","көйгөй бар","kuy-GUY bar"],["there is no water","суу жок","soo zhok"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Verb stem + а / е / й + person ending. Келүү (to come): кел-е-м."],"rows":[["I come","келем","keh-LEM"],["you come","келесиң","keh-leh-SEENG"],["he / she comes","келет","keh-LET"],["we come","келебиз","keh-leh-BEEZ"],["you come (formal)","келесиз","keh-leh-SEEZ"],["they come","келишет","keh-lee-SHET"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","мен нан жеп жатам","men nan zhep zhah-TAM"],["you are reading a book","сен китеп окуп жатасың","sen kee-TEP o-KOOP zhah-tah-SUHNG"],["she works in a bank","ал банкта иштейт","al bank-TAH eesh-TAYT"],["we drink tea","биз чай ичебиз","beez chai ee-cheh-BEEZ"],["they are sleeping","алар уктап жатышат","ah-LAR ook-TAP zhah-tuh-SHAT"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb goes last. Order: who, where or when, what, verb. Kyrgyz has no articles: \"китеп\" means \"a book\" or \"the book\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","мен китеп окуйм","men kee-TEP o-KUIM"],["she drinks tea","ал чай ичет","al chai ee-CHET"],["we go to school","биз мектепке барабыз","beez mek-tep-KEH bah-rah-BUHZ"]],"ex":[["I read a book","мен китеп окуйм","men kee-TEP o-KUIM"],["he drinks tea","ал чай ичет","al chai ee-CHET"],["we go to school","биз мектепке барабыз","beez mek-tep-KEH bah-rah-BUHZ"],["they eat bread","алар нан жешет","ah-LAR nan zhe-SHET"],["the teacher writes","мугалим жазат","moo-gah-LEEM zhah-ZAT"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put -ба / -бе / -па / -пе / -бо / -бө / -по / -пө after the verb stem: барам (I go), барбайм (I do not go). For nouns use \"эмес\" (is not). \"Жок\" means \"there is not\". Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["I go","барам","bah-RAM"],["I do not go","барбайм","bar-BAIM"],["is","(no ending)","-"],["is not","эмес","eh-MES"]],"ex":[["I want","мен каалайм","men kah-LAIM"],["I do not want","мен каалабайм","men kah-lah-BAIM"],["I speak English","мен англисче сүйлөйм","men ahn-glees-CHEH sewy-LUIM"],["I do not speak English","мен англисче сүйлөбөйм","men ahn-glees-CHEH sewy-lur-BUIM"],["I like it","мага жагат","mah-GAH zhah-GAT"],["I do not like it","мага жакпайт","mah-GAH zhak-PAIT"],["she is here","ал бул жерде","al bool zher-DEH"],["she is not here","ал бул жерде эмес","al bool zher-DEH eh-MES"],["I have a car","менде машина бар","men-DEH mah-SHEE-nah bar"],["I do not have a car","менде машина жок","men-DEH mah-SHEE-nah zhok"],["I understand","түшүнөм","tew-shew-NUM"],["I do not understand","түшүнбөйм","tew-shewn-BUIM"],["we are tired","биз чарчагандабыз","beez char-chah-gan-dah-BUHZ"],["we are not tired","биз чарчаган жокпуз","beez char-chah-GAN zhok-POOZ"],["he works on Sundays","ал жекшемби күнү иштейт","al zhek-shem-BEE kew-NEW eesh-TAYT"],["he does not work on Sundays","ал жекшемби күнү иштебейт","al zhek-shem-BEE kew-NEW eesh-teh-BAYT"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add the little word -бы / -би / -бу / -бү / -пы / -пи after the word you are asking about. It is the same for every question."],"rows":[["you are a student","сиз студентсиз","seez stoo-dent-SEEZ"],["are you a student?","сиз студентсизби?","seez stoo-dent-seez-BEE"],["he is here","ал бул жерде","al bool zher-DEH"],["is he here?","ал бул жердеби?","al bool zher-deh-BEE"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","бул сиздин китебиңизби?","bool seez-DEEN kee-teh-beeng-eez-BEE"],["are they here?","алар бул жердеби?","ah-LAR bool zher-deh-BEE"],["do you like tea?","сиз чайды жакшы көрөсүзбү?","seez chai-DUH zhak-SHUH kur-rur-sewz-BEW"],["is it cold?","суукпу?","soo-ook-POO"],["do you speak English?","сиз англисче сүйлөйсүзбү?","seez ahn-glees-CHEH sewy-lur-sewz-BEW"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words stand where the answer would stand."],"rows":[["what","эмне","em-NEH"],["who","ким","keem"],["where","кайда","kai-DAH"],["when","качан","kah-CHAN"],["why","эмне үчүн","em-NEH ew-CHEWN"],["how","кандай","kan-DAI"],["how much","канча","kan-CHAH"],["which","кайсы","kai-SUH"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","атыңыз ким?","ah-tuhng-UHZ KEEM"],["who is he?","ал ким?","al KEEM"],["where do you live?","сиз кайда жашайсыз?","seez kai-DAH zhah-shai-SUHZ"],["when is the lesson?","сабак качан?","sah-BAK kah-CHAN"],["why are you late?","эмне үчүн кечикдиңиз?","em-NEH ew-CHEWN keh-cheek-deeng-EEZ"],["how are you?","кандайсыз?","kan-dai-SUHZ"],["how much is it?","канча турат?","kan-CHAH too-RAT"],["which book?","кайсы китеп?","kai-SUH kee-TEP"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Endings go on the noun: -ым / -им (my), -ың / -иң (your), -ы / -и (his / her). To say you like something, use \"мага жагат\" (to me it is pleasing)."],"rows":[["my book","китебим","kee-teh-BEEM"],["your book","китебиң","kee-teh-BEENG"],["his / her book","китеби","kee-teh-BEE"],["our book","китебибиз","kee-teh-bee-BEEZ"],["your book (formal)","китебиңиз","kee-teh-beeng-EEZ"]],"ex":[["my phone","телефоным","teh-leh-fo-NUHM"],["your house (formal)","үйүңүз","ewy-ewng-EWZ"],["his sister","анын сиңдиси","ah-NUHN sing-dee-SEE"],["I like music","мага музыка жагат","mah-GAH moo-zuh-KAH zhah-GAT"],["I love football","мен футболду жакшы көрөм","men foot-bol-DOO zhak-SHUH kur-RUM"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["сен (informal): friends, family, children. сиз (formal): strangers, older people, work. Verb endings change: -сың (informal), -сыз (formal)."],"rows":[["how are you?","кандайсың? / кандайсыз?","kan-dai-SUHNG / kan-dai-SUHZ"],["you speak","сүйлөйсүң / сүйлөйсүз","sewy-lur-SEWNG / sewy-lur-SEWZ"],["your name","атың / атыңыз","ah-TUHNG / ah-tuhng-UHZ"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","кандайсың?","kan-dai-SUHNG"],["how are you? (formal)","кандайсыз?","kan-dai-SUHZ"],["where are you going? (informal)","кайда барасың?","kai-DAH bah-rah-SUHNG"],["where are you going? (formal)","кайда барасыз?","kai-DAH bah-rah-SUHZ"],["please sit down (formal)","отуруңуз, сураныч","o-too-roong-OOZ soo-rah-NUHCH"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: -ды / -ди / -ты / -ти + person ending (бардым = I went). Future uses the present form with a time word: эртең барам (tomorrow I go)."],"rows":[["I went","бардым","bar-DUHM"],["you went","бардың","bar-DUHNG"],["he went","барды","bar-DUH"],["we went","бардык","bar-DUHK"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","кечээ чарчадым","keh-CHEH char-chah-DUHM"],["I will study tomorrow","эртең окуйм","er-TENG o-KUIM"],["we went to the park","биз паркка бардык","beez park-KAH bar-DUHK"],["I saw him","мен аны көрдүм","men ah-NUH kurd-EWM"],["she wrote a letter","ал кат жазды","al kat zhaz-DUH"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: the bare verb stem. Formal: add -ыңыз / -иңиз. To forbid, add -ба / -бе after the stem."],"rows":[["come (informal)","кел","kel"],["come (formal)","келиңиз","keh-leeng-EEZ"],["do not come","келбе","kel-BEH"],["sit down","отур","o-TOOR"]],"ex":[["come here","бул жакка кел","bool zhak-KAH KEL"],["do not come here","бул жакка келбе","bool zhak-KAH kel-BEH"],["sit down","отур","o-TOOR"],["do not sit down","отурба","o-toor-BAH"],["be quiet","унчукпа","oon-chook-PAH"],["do not be late","кечикпе","keh-cheek-PEH"],["open the door","эшикти ач","eh-sheek-TEE ACH"],["close the window","терезени жап","teh-reh-zeh-NEE ZHAP"],["listen to me","мени ук","meh-NEE OOK"],["do not worry","тынчсызданба","tuhnch-suhz-dahn-BAH"],["speak slowly","жай сүйлө","zhai sewy-LUR"],["wait a moment","бир аз күт","beer AZ KEWT"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Can: verb + а алуу (сүзө алам, I can swim). Must: \"керек\" (needed). Want: -гым келет (жегим келет, I want to eat)."],"rows":[["I can swim","сүзө алам","sew-ZUR ah-LAM"],["I cannot swim","сүзө албайм","sew-ZUR al-BAIM"],["I must go","баруум керек","bah-roo-OOM keh-REK"],["I want to go","баргым келет","bar-GUHM keh-LET"]],"ex":[["I can swim","мен сүзө алам","men sew-ZUR ah-LAM"],["I cannot swim","мен сүзө албайм","men sew-ZUR al-BAIM"],["can you help me?","мага жардам бере аласызбы?","mah-GAH zhar-DAM beh-REH ah-lah-suhz-BUH"],["we must go","биз барышыбыз керек","beez bah-ruh-shuh-BUHZ keh-REK"],["we must not go","биз барбашыбыз керек","beez bar-bah-shuh-BUHZ keh-REK"],["I want to eat","жегим келет","zheh-GEEM keh-LET"],["I do not want to eat","жегим келбейт","zheh-GEEM kel-BAYT"],["you can come","келсеңиз болот","kel-seng-EEZ bo-LOT"],["you cannot come","келсеңиз болбойт","kel-seng-EEZ bol-BOIT"],["she wants to study","анын окугусу келет","ah-NUHN o-koo-goo-SOO keh-LET"],["I must work today","бүгүн иштешим керек","bew-GEWN eesh-teh-SHEEM keh-REK"],["you must not run","жүгүргө болбойт","zhew-gewr-GUR bol-BOIT"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Kyrgyz uses endings, not words in front: -да / -де (in, on, at), -га / -ге (to), -дан / -ден (from), -дын / -дин (of)."],"rows":[["in / on / at","-да / -де","dah / deh"],["to","-га / -ге","gah / geh"],["from","-дан / -ден","dan / den"],["of","-дын / -дин","duhn / deen"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","китеп үстөлдө","kee-TEP ews-tul-DUR"],["the cat is under the table","мышык үстөлдүн астында","muh-SHUHK ews-tul-DEWN as-tuhn-DAH"],["I am at school","мен мектептемин","men mek-tep-teh-MEEN"],["I am at home","мен үйдөмүн","men ewy-dur-MEWN"],["